WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.121
What is inside a FIT file from your watch.

2
00:00:05.621 --> 00:00:11.558
The binary format behind every Garmin, Wahoo and Coros workout, how to turn

3
00:00:11.558 --> 00:00:17.337
it into CSV or GPX, and how heart rate zones and training load are worked

4
00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:17.653
out.

5
00:00:19.053 --> 00:00:24.941
What a FIT file is. FIT means Flexible and Interoperable Data Transfer.

6
00:00:26.241 --> 00:00:28.303
Heart rate zones in plain words.

7
00:00:28.303 --> 00:00:32.620
Zones are bands of heart rate that match different kinds of effort.

8
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.117
Time in zone and training load.

9
00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:41.148
Heart Rate Zones takes a workout file and adds up the seconds you spent

10
00:00:41.148 --> 00:00:42.069
in each zone.

11
00:00:43.369 --> 00:00:48.201
Why read it locally. Workout files show where you live, the routes you take,

12
00:00:48.201 --> 00:00:49.727
and when you leave home.

13
00:00:51.027 --> 00:00:55.368
To try it, open FIT File Converter & Viewer in OpenFile.

14
00:00:55.368 --> 00:00:59.787
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

15
00:00:59.787 --> 00:01:03.741
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

16
00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:09.729
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
